The animated text effect was showing all three words (DE, TU, TIERRA) simultaneously instead of cycling through them one at a time.

## Changes

- **HTML**: Wrapped word elements in `.words-slider` container to animate as a unit
- **CSS**: Moved animation from individual `.word` elements to `.words-slider` wrapper
- **Animation keyframes**: Changed from percentage-based (`-100%`, `-200%`) to pixel-based translations (`-40px`, `-80px`) to properly offset each 40px-tall word

## Technical Details

Before: Each word had `height: 100%` and its own animation, causing all three to move identically and overlap.

After: Fixed-height words in an animated slider that translates vertically:

```css
.words {
    overflow: hidden;
    height: 40px;  /* Shows one word at a time */
}

.words-slider {
    animation: spin_words 9s infinite;
}

.word {
    display: block;
    height: 40px;  /* Stack vertically */
}

@keyframes spin_words {
    0%, 28%   { transform: translateY(0); }        /* DE visible */
    33%, 61%  { transform: translateY(-40px); }    /* TU visible */
    66%, 94%  { transform: translateY(-80px); }    /* TIERRA visible */
}
```

Result: Animation now properly cycles "PRODUCTO **DE**" → "PRODUCTO **TU**" → "PRODUCTO **TIERRA**" every 9 seconds.

