The invite tracker stopped sending messages to `#invitations` due to missing permission validation and inconsistent invite detection logic.

## Changes

### New: `utils/inviteHelper.js`
- Extracted `getInviter(guild, member, cachedInvites)` for invite detection
- Compares cached vs. current invite uses to identify which invite was used
- Returns inviter User object or null if undetectable

### Updated: `bot.js` - `guildMemberAdd` event
Rewrote event handler with defensive checks:

```javascript
client.on('guildMemberAdd', async (member) => {
    console.log(`[DEBUG] ${member.user.tag} joined.`);

    const inviter = await getInviter(member.guild, member, invites.get(guildId));
    if (!inviter) {
        console.warn(`[WARNING] Failed to detect inviter for user ${member.user.tag}`);
        return;
    }

    const isDuplicate = await db.checkInviteHistory(inviter.id, member.id);
    if (isDuplicate) {
        await sendDuplicateInviteNotification(client, member, inviter.id);
        return;
    }

    // Create users, add history, increment count, reward LC
    const updatedData = await db.incrementInvites(inviter.id);
    await db.updateBalance(inviter.id, config.currency.inviteReward, 'invite_reward');
    await db.updateBalance(member.id, config.currency.inviteReward, 'invite_joined');

    // Permission check before sending
    const permissions = inviteChannel.permissionsFor(client.user);
    if (!permissions?.has(PermissionsBitField.Flags.SendMessages)) {
        console.error('[ERROR] Bot lacks SendMessages permission');
        return;
    }

    await inviteChannel.send(/* ... */);
});
```

### Updated: `sendDuplicateInviteNotification`
- Added SendMessages permission check before sending
- Uses `guild.channels.cache.get()` for consistency
- Logs missing permissions with `[ERROR]` prefix

### Logging standardization
- `[DEBUG]`: Normal operations (9 instances)
- `[WARNING]`: Missing data/inviter detection failures (3 instances)  
- `[ERROR]`: Permission failures, channel not found (3 instances)

### Transaction type consistency
- Inviter: `'invite_reward'` (both updateBalance and recordTransaction)
- Invited: `'invite_joined'` (both updateBalance and recordTransaction)

## Tests

**`test-invite-tracker.js`**: Validates `getInviter()` edge cases (invite use changes, no changes, new invites)

**`test-invite-integration.js`**: Validates complete implementation structure (exports, config, permissions, database functions, logging format)

