This allows clients to use properties from multiple vault sources that end in the same key, e.g. `foo/bar/application` and `bar/baz/application`.

Without this change, composite vault sources can't have the same key (application name, profile, …):

```yaml
spring.cloud.config.server.composite:
  - type: vault
    # ...
    backend: vault/path/a
  - type: vault
    # ...
    backend: vault/path/a
```

```
{
 "name": "app-name",
  "profiles": [
    "default",
    "some-profile"
  ],
  "propertySources": [
   {
      "name": "vault:some-profile",
      "source": {
        "spring.datasource.username": "some-application"
        "hello": "from /vault/path/a/some-profile"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "vault:some-profile",
      "source": {
        "hello": "from /vault/path/b/some-profile"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

With this patch, the source name contains the full name (e.g. `vault:path/b/some-profile`) similar to the yaml sources (e.g. `/root/path/app/application.yaml`).

The Byzantine evidence ID generation used XOR operations on validator key, block height, and evidence type. This created a collision vulnerability: same validator with different evidence types at the same height would generate IDs differing by only one byte (type discriminant at position 8).

## Changes

- **Evidence ID generation**: Replaced XOR composition with Blake3 cryptographic hash over all components (validator key, block height, evidence type, timestamp)
- **Test coverage**: Added `test_evidence_id_uniqueness_different_types_same_height` to verify collision resistance

## Before
```rust
let mut id = [0u8; 32];
id[..32].copy_from_slice(&evidence.validator.key_id);
for i in 0..8 {
    id[i] ^= height_bytes[i];
}
id[8] ^= type_discriminant;
```

## After
```rust
let mut hasher = blake3::Hasher::new();
hasher.update(&evidence.validator.key_id);
hasher.update(&evidence.block_height.to_le_bytes());
hasher.update(&[type_discriminant]);
hasher.update(&evidence.recorded_at.to_le_bytes());
let hash = hasher.finalize();
```

This prevents attackers from strategically triggering different evidence types to create ID collisions.

